# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# openimis-fe_js/script/entrypoint.sh and openimis-be_py/script/entrypoint.sh are
# COPYed into Linux images and run by bash. A CRLF checkout produces
#   /script/entrypoint.sh: line 35: syntax error near unexpected token $'do\r'
# and the container exits immediately.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for files interpreted inside containers.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.env text eol=lf

# Fonts are binary. A CRLF "fix" applied to a woff2 corrupts it, and the
# failure is silent: the browser rejects the file and falls back to a system
# font, which is the exact bug this font was added to fix.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
